# SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000135  -  CAT I
# The web server must generate a unique session identifier for each session
# using a FIPS 140-2 approved random number generator.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000135
group:           V-206399
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
cci:             CCI-001188
control_rev5:    SC-23

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise can be placed in FIPS mode, which constrains the
                 instance to the algorithms and restrictions of FIPS Publication 140-2,
                 including the random number generator behind session identifier
                 generation. The generator itself is not configurable; enabling FIPS mode
                 is the whole of the application's contribution.

governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        FIPS mode must be enabled during initial installation; enabling it
                 afterward requires a reinstall or upgrade of the application -
                 installation procedure, per the SPLK-CL-000390 fix text
external:        The validated cryptographic module and kernel FIPS mode on the host -
                 operating system
external:        Uniqueness and non-sequential form of the issued identifiers, which the
                 check verifies by comparing two users' session IDs - a product
                 implementation property with no configuration surface

citation:        splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-116 (SPLUNK_FIPS = [0|1], whether the instance
                 operates in Federal Information Processing Standards mode and uses the
                 algorithms and restrictions that apply to the FIPS Publication 140-2
                 standard); corroborated by the product STIG fix for SPLK-CL-000390, which
                 sets SPLUNK_FIPS=1 in splunk-launch.conf before the initial start
finding:         FIPS mode is not enabled (SPLUNK_FIPS is unset or 0), so the instance is
                 not constrained to FIPS 140-2 approved algorithms for session identifier
                 generation, which is the application's only contribution to this
                 requirement.
